---
title: "12 · Everything at once (H3)"
lesson: "Three shots, three transitions, rolled camera and weather, two voices in two languages. The compiler computes timestamps, speaker IDs and <d> tags, and lints the result against the official guide."
tags: [tutorial, h3, woah]
---
@h3 t2va 16:9
style: live-action, cinematic
$keeper = __creature__

SHOT 4s | pull out, small, slow
A lighthouse keeper's kitchen at the edge of the world. Beyond the windows, __weather__ over a black sea. A $keeper in a knitted scarf pours tea for two.
KEEPER (warm, raspy old voice): The ships stopped coming years ago.
SFX: a kettle hisses; wind worries the shutters

SHOT 3s | cut, __camera__
A close-up of the second teacup, steam curling up, the chair across the table still empty.
SFX: a clock ticks

SHOT 4s | dissolve, arc, slow
the empty chair, now holding a translucent woman made of sea spray who smiles at the $keeper.
GHOST (soft, echoing voice): [French] Je suis toujours venue.
KEEPER: I know.
SFX: waves swell far below; a single gull cries

MUSIC: a music box melody at a slow tempo, joined by sustained low strings that rise and then fade
